The downstream evidence is now coherent: Copilot did eventually produce a valid two-file draft PR, but the kickoff ledger was a one-time snapshot and had no PR-driven reconciliation path. Separately, the GPT Master run never entered its jobs (`action_required` at creation time); even after approval, its explicit all-reports-complete gate would reject this cycle because GPT and Gemini were both `INCOMPLETE`.
